<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 150 0 R
/T (Why the measures and metrics support the usability evaluation goals:)
/E (Why the measures and metrics support the usability evaluation goals:)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
310 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 150 0 R
/E (The measures and metrics outlined for the usability evaluation are crucial for assessing the effectiveness of the interface. By measuring efficiency through the time to complete tasks and the number of steps taken, we can identify potential areas for improvement in the design. The task success rate will reveal how well participants can navigate the interface, while both participant and observer perceptions will provide insights into the usability of the system. Tracking failure and success rates will help us understand if users needed assistance and whether they gave up on tasks. Additionally, the error rate will highlight common mistakes, informing necessary adjustments. Finally, post-task surveys and interviews will measure ease of use and overall satisfaction, enabling us to provide comprehensive feedback on the interface's usability. )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
