596 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1432 0 R
/E (The WHO Mortality Database is a comprehensive data intensive information system that specifically compiles worldwide mortality statistics. WHO uses data collected from health registration systems in order to provide access to comprehensive global mortality statistics organized by various demographic factors such as: Geographical Location \(Country\), Year, Age, and Sex. The Mortality Database is vital for researchers, public health officials, epidemiologists, the public, and policymakers to provide insight and understanding of global health trends, the burden of diseases, and Mortality patterns. )
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
597 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1433 0 R
/E (The WHO Mortality Database interface allows users to access and analyze mortality data through various queries that provide visualizations, reports, and information to better understand trends over time. )
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
