623 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 168 0 R
/T (Identify the goals for conducting the usability evaluation: The purpose of this usability evaluation is to assess how effectively the WHO Mortality Database helps users achieve their objectives in exploring global mortality data. By identifying potential usability challenges and evaluating the platform's design, we aim to improve users' ability to gather, interpret, and analyze the data relevant to their research or decision-making needs. This evaluation will focus on ensuring that users can easily access, filter, and comprehend critical information without facing unnecessary obstacles.)
/E (Identify the goals for conducting the usability evaluation: The purpose of this usability evaluation is to assess how effectively the WHO Mortality Database helps users achieve their objectives in exploring global mortality data. By identifying potential usability challenges and evaluating the platform's design, we aim to improve users' ability to gather, interpret, and analyze the data relevant to their research or decision-making needs. This evaluation will focus on ensuring that users can easily access, filter, and comprehend critical information without facing unnecessary obstacles.)
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
624 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 168 0 R
/E (Goal # 1: Assess Usability and Navigability of the WHO Mortality Database.)
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
625 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 168 0 R
/E (Users visit the WHO Mortality Database to extract insights into global mortality trends. This goal emphasizes evaluating how intuitively users can search for and retrieve relevant data, such as mortality statistics for specific age groups and diseases. For instance, users might need to quickly filter mortality data by cause, location, or age group, like the number of deaths from non-communicable diseases for ages 15-24 and 35-54 in Japan. Ensuring that the platform allows easy access to these features will empower users to gather and interpret the data they need efficiently.)
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
